    a: "ps aux lists running processes; top/htop shows a live, resource-sorted view; kill <pid> sends a signal (default SIGTERM, a polite exit request; kill -9 is SIGKILL, immediate/forceful, for a process ignoring SIGTERM); systemctl status/start/stop/restart/enable manages services under systemd, and journalctl -u <service> shows that service's logs.",
