    lvl: "med",
    q: "A user's home directory redirection (Folder Redirection GPO) is causing extremely slow logon times over a VPN connection. Diagnose and propose a fix.",
    sol: "Folder Redirection synchronously accesses files over the network at logon by default — over a VPN's typically lower bandwidth/higher latency link than the LAN it was designed for, this can add minutes to logon. Fixes: enable Offline Files so redirected folders are cached locally and sync in the background rather than blocking logon; exclude VPN-connecting users from synchronous redirection processing; or move to OneDrive Known Folder Move instead of classic Folder Redirection, since its sync model is designed for exactly this remote-heavy scenario.",
    exp: "Folder Redirection was designed assuming LAN-speed connectivity — remote/VPN users routinely hit this specific, well-known pain point, and it's why many orgs have moved to OneDrive Known Folder Move for remote-heavy workforces.",
